.TITLE "df"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Reports disk space usage on macOS filesystems. This command displays the amount
of available and used disk space for mounted filesystems. It provides an
overview of storage utilization, which is essential for __system monitoring__
and managing disk resources.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**diskfree**

.DIV "TLDR"
**df -h**
Displays disk space usage in human-readable format (e.g., GB, MB).
> __-h__: human-readable flag

**df -i**
Displays inode usage (number of used and free inodes) for filesystems.
> __-i__: inodes flag

**df __/path/to/volume__**
Displays disk space usage for the filesystem containing __/path/to/volume__.
> __/path/to/volume__: A path within the target filesystem.

**df -T**
Includes the filesystem type in the output.
> __-T__: filesystem type flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
`df` is crucial for quickly assessing disk space availability. On macOS,
you'll typically see filesystems like `APFS` or `devfs`. Combine with `-h`
for easy-to-read output. For more detailed per-directory usage, use `du`.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:du** **mac:diskutil**

documentation: https://ss64.com/osx/df.html
